12. In the Cartesian coordinate system $x O y$, it is known that points $A_{1}(-2,0), A_{2}(2,0)$, and a moving point $P(x, y)$ satisfies the product of the slopes of lines $A_{1} P$ and $A_{2} P$ is $-\frac{3}{4}$. Let the trajectory of point $P$ be curve $C$.
(1) Find the equation of $C$;
(2) Suppose point $M$ is on the line $x=4$, and two lines passing through $M$ intersect $C$ at points $A, B$ and $P, Q$ respectively, and $|M A| \cdot|M B| = |M P| \cdot|M Q|$. Find the sum of the slopes of lines $A B$ and $P Q$.

11. Given a sequence $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ whose terms are all non-negative, the sum of its first $n$ terms is $S_{n}$, and for any $n \in N^{*}$, we have
$$
a_{n+1} \leq \frac{a_{n}+a_{n+2}}{2} \text {. }
$$
(1) If $a_{1}=1, a_{505}=2017$, find the maximum value of $a_{6}$;
(2) If for any $n \in N^{*}$, we have $S_{n} \leq 1$, prove that $0 \leq a_{n}-a_{n+1} \leq \frac{2}{n(n+1)}$.

4. (8 points) $A$, $B$, and $C$ are picking watermelons.
The sum of the number of watermelons picked by $A$ and $B$ is 6 less than that picked by $C$;
The sum of the number of watermelons picked by $B$ and $C$ is 16 more than that picked by $A$;
The sum of the number of watermelons picked by $C$ and $A$ is 8 more than that picked by $B$;
How many watermelons did they pick in total? $\qquad$

