Célia wants to trade stickers with Guilherme from an album about Brazilian animals. Célia wants to trade four butterfly stickers, five shark stickers, three snake stickers, six parakeet stickers, and six monkey stickers. All of Guilherme's stickers are of spiders. They know that

(a) one butterfly sticker is worth three shark stickers;

(b) one snake sticker is worth three parakeet stickers;

(c) one monkey sticker is worth four spider stickers;

(d) one parakeet sticker is worth three spider stickers;

(e) one shark sticker is worth two parakeet stickers.

How many stickers can Célia receive if she trades all the ones she wants?

